# Product Objectives

## High Volatility 
Design the mechanics to naturally force players to negotiate, form temporary alliances, and inevitably betray each other through mechanics like the "Clubs" RNG damage or the "Forced All-In" card.

## User Testing Goal
Conduct local pass-and-play or sessions to balance the base damage of Poker hands versus the power of the 24 Special Cards.

---

# Gameplay Pillars

## Structured Start, Explosive Finish
The game guarantees a perfectly balanced starting hand (one of each suit, a non-duplicate nine, one random), ensuring a fair early game, but ramps into absolute chaos by Round 8.

## Reactive Retaliation (Berserk)
Players should never feel entirely defenseless. If the table gangs up on one player, the Berserk system arms that player with double attacks or immediate turn-interrupts to exact revenge.

## Strategic Build Paths
Through the Suit Identity System, players must sacrifice 4 cards from their usable pool to permanently lock in a playstyle (e.g., Spades for chip damage, Hearts for death negation). 

## High Swing Potential
Standard attacks deal chip damage, but perfectly executed combos (like a Straight Flush halving a target's HP, or the Void card permanently banning a mechanic) can flip the state of the board in a single turn.

---

# Unique Selling Points

## Poker-Scaling Combat
Instead of standard "Attack = 5" cards, players play up to 5 cards per attack, utilizing actual Poker hands (Pairs, Triples, Straights) to mathematically scale their damage output.

## The Berserk State Machine Interrupt
Unlike standard turn-based games, the turn order is not safe. The ability to push a hijacked turn onto the stack creates unparalleled table tension.

## The Joker Class Mutation
Instead of players picking classes at the start menu, the "Joker" is a physical card injected into the deck mid-game. Drawing it allows a player to physically mutate their ruleset, gaining new max HP, passive chip damage, and dice-roll abilities.

## The Four 10s Ultimatum
A unique exodia-style mechanic where playing four 10s stops the game and forces the player to make a massive choice: fully heal but take +50% damage forever, or instantly wipe 20% of the entire table's HP.

